From c24e2a3b2b69af9082514aa9bbb89eb0b6701450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: l4h <z@univalence.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:30:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] tcb: add seL4_TCB_ReadFPU and seL4_TCB_WriteFPU

Allow a holder of a TCB capability to read or replace the thread's
floating point / vector register state via a frame it owns. This is
needed by user-level OS personalities (signal frames, ptrace, fork) that
manage threads running foreign code.

Any live copy of the state is flushed (possibly from a remote core) before
the transfer, and loaded again afterwards if the target is the caller
itself: it returns to user level without passing through switchToThread(),
which is where the FPU is loaded, and would otherwise fault on its next
FPU instruction. (A target running on another core has been stalled off
it, as for every TCB invocation.) Images written by user level are
sanitised so that loading them cannot fault in the kernel; on x86, MXCSR
is masked with the CPU's MXCSR_MASK, read with FXSAVE at boot.
